1
00:00:04,504 --> 00:00:05,588
Lisbon...

2
00:00:07,131 --> 00:00:09,884
It's over. It's done.

3
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:14,180
I just want you to know
I'm okay.

4
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:17,808
And I'm gonna miss you.

5
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:25,942
And that's what police do.

6
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:27,568
We help people that are in trouble

7
00:00:27,693 --> 00:00:29,820
and we stop people
from making trouble.

8
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:31,572
It's a hard job sometimes

9
00:00:31,697 --> 00:00:33,616
but I think it's
the best job there is.

10
00:00:34,116 --> 00:00:35,159
What about you?

11
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:37,870
Does anybody want to be
a police officer when they grow up?

12
00:00:40,289 --> 00:00:42,166
Well, there's time to think about it.

13
00:00:43,417 --> 00:00:44,460
Any questions?

14
00:00:44,585 --> 00:00:47,296
Oh, oh, oh! Oh!
Oh, oh!

15
00:00:47,463 --> 00:00:48,923
Did you ever shoot somebody?

16
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,009
Well, actually, yes.

17
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:54,053
Did they die?

18
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,847
Point is, there are
bad people in the world.

19
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,683
Not all, but some.

20
00:00:59,183 --> 00:01:02,061
"And sometimes you have
to do things you don't wanna do"

21
00:01:02,186 --> 00:01:03,813
"to make sure worse things
don't happen."

22
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:07,191
- "Was there lots of blood?"
- "I'm afraid that's all the time we have."

23
00:01:07,358 --> 00:01:11,904
- "What do we say?"
- "Thank you, chief Lisbon!"

24
00:01:35,886 --> 00:01:37,054
Hey, Henry, what's up?

25
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:38,889
There's a man here
wants to speak with you.

26
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:42,560
An Agent Abbott
uh, with the FBI.

27
00:01:42,768 --> 00:01:44,812
- Abbott?
- That's what he said.

28
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:46,731
- Send him in.
- Okay.

29
00:01:57,074 --> 00:01:58,117
Yes?

30
00:01:58,451 --> 00:01:59,702
"Do you want me
to send him in now?"

31
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:00,911
Yes.

32
00:02:08,669 --> 00:02:09,754
Hi, Lisbon.

33
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:11,922
Hmm.

34
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:17,261
Well, you... have a nice place.

35
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:19,263
Hmm?

36
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,390
You've been here, what, 18 months?

37
00:02:31,734 --> 00:02:33,861
- Have you heard from Jane?
- Nope.

38
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:38,324
Nothing? No email
no phone call?

39
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:39,659
No.

40
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:41,077
Hmm.

41
00:02:41,827 --> 00:02:44,413
What about Rigsby
or Van Pelt?

42
00:02:44,538 --> 00:02:46,165
Have they heard anything?

43
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:47,625
I'm having dinner with them soon.

44
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:49,960
Why don't you join us?
You could ask them yourself.

45
00:02:50,211 --> 00:02:51,879
Mm-hmm. And Cho?

46
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:54,006
Haven't heard from him in ages.

47
00:02:55,341 --> 00:02:58,511
I don't know where Jane is
and Frankly, I don't care.

48
00:02:58,719 --> 00:03:00,388
No? Well...

49
00:03:01,263 --> 00:03:02,765
You two were so close.

50
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,309
It was a long time ago.

51
00:03:07,895 --> 00:03:09,689
When are you guys gonna
give up chasing him?

52
00:03:09,855 --> 00:03:12,274
Oh, we're the FBI.
We don't give up.

53
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:20,950
That is a nice shell.

54
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:23,911
It's a cowrie.

55
00:03:25,121 --> 00:03:26,163
Oh.

56
00:03:27,039 --> 00:03:28,374
- May I?
- Sure.

57
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:36,632
You know, they say a shell
always carries around

58
00:03:36,757 --> 00:03:38,175
the sound of the ocean with it.

59
00:03:44,181 --> 00:03:45,224
Ah.

60
00:05:09,556 --> 00:05:10,808
{\an8}"Dear Lisbon"

61
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:13,519
{\an8}"I hope this finds you well."

62
00:05:15,771 --> 00:05:17,105
{\an8}"All's well here."

63
00:05:19,858 --> 00:05:21,276
"I have my routines."

64
00:05:22,945 --> 00:05:24,488
{\an8}"Weather's finally turned."

65
00:05:25,572 --> 00:05:27,074
{\an8}"It's a little cooler."

66
00:05:27,324 --> 00:05:28,617
{\an8}"Far from cold."

67
00:05:31,119 --> 00:05:32,329
{\an8}"The ocean's still warm."

68
00:05:33,413 --> 00:05:37,417
{\an8}"And with the warm ocean currents
comes an abundance of sea life."

69
00:05:39,670 --> 00:05:43,340
{\an8}"Just yesterday, I watched a pot
of dolphins play so close to shore"

70
00:05:43,507 --> 00:05:44,842
{\an8}"I could almost touch them."

71
00:05:46,885 --> 00:05:48,971
{\an8}"They're the kind of things
I think you'd enjoy."

72
00:06:57,789 --> 00:06:58,999
Unbelievable.

73
00:07:00,042 --> 00:07:02,419
Cheaper than yesterday, but more
expensive than last week.

74
00:07:32,866 --> 00:07:34,618
Patrick! Patrick!

75
00:07:37,746 --> 00:07:39,039
Oh, really, guys?

76
00:07:45,837 --> 00:07:48,715
Very persistent, I must say.
Very persistent.

77
00:07:56,223 --> 00:07:57,683
Huh? What have we got here?

78
00:07:58,934 --> 00:08:00,102
Yeah.

79
00:08:08,068 --> 00:08:09,361
"Where is it?"

80
00:08:21,081 --> 00:08:22,124
Hey!

81
00:08:32,551 --> 00:08:33,593
What are you looking at?

82
00:08:35,887 --> 00:08:36,930
Nothing.

83
00:08:45,313 --> 00:08:46,523
"Good morning", Victor.

84
00:08:47,441 --> 00:08:49,651
"Ah, Mr. Jane. Good morning."

85
00:08:58,952 --> 00:09:01,288
No, no, no, no,
no, no.

86
00:09:12,424 --> 00:09:14,634
"Cha... Charre...
charreteras?"

87
00:09:14,926 --> 00:09:15,969
What... uh...

88
00:09:16,094 --> 00:09:18,138
"Charreteras. Charreteras.
Charreteras."

89
00:09:18,263 --> 00:09:19,306
"Yes."

90
00:09:19,431 --> 00:09:21,183
- "What are they called?"
- Ah, epaulettes.

91
00:09:21,308 --> 00:09:23,060
{\an8}Epaulettes. "Charreteras."

92
00:09:28,356 --> 00:09:29,816
"Yes. Yes."

93
00:09:32,778 --> 00:09:33,820
{\an8}Ah!

94
00:10:02,933 --> 00:10:04,309
Hey, Hugo.

95
00:10:04,559 --> 00:10:06,937
How you doing, boy?
Good? Good, Hugo?

96
00:10:07,312 --> 00:10:08,605
Good boy.

97
00:10:09,856 --> 00:10:10,899
{\an8}Alfredo...

98
00:10:37,843 --> 00:10:38,885
Hi.

99
00:10:40,387 --> 00:10:41,429
Hello.

100
00:10:41,930 --> 00:10:42,973
From the US?

101
00:10:43,181 --> 00:10:45,100
You weren't fooled
by my impeccable Spanish?

102
00:10:45,559 --> 00:10:47,394
No. Anyway...

103
00:10:47,978 --> 00:10:49,521
You're reading. Sorry.

104
00:10:56,194 --> 00:10:59,281
Thing is, uh...
I miss speaking English.

105
00:11:00,699 --> 00:11:02,284
Roger's the only other
English speaker

106
00:11:02,409 --> 00:11:04,828
and he's... well, he's not
a great talker.

107
00:11:05,370 --> 00:11:07,873
Turns out being understood
is an underrated pleasure.

108
00:11:08,165 --> 00:11:09,457
- I can imagine.
- Mm.

109
00:11:11,251 --> 00:11:12,460
I'll leave you alone.

110
00:11:13,336 --> 00:11:14,379
No problem.

111
00:11:21,678 --> 00:11:23,138
Looks like you're nearly finished.

112
00:11:23,722 --> 00:11:25,098
Do you want it when I'm finished?

113
00:11:25,765 --> 00:11:26,808
I wouldn't mind it.

114
00:11:27,726 --> 00:11:29,686
It's not easy to get books
in English around here.

115
00:11:30,353 --> 00:11:31,396
Okay.

116
00:11:33,064 --> 00:11:35,358
- Is it any good?
- You like murder mysteries?

117
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:38,153
Not really.

118
00:11:39,070 --> 00:11:41,573
- Then you probably won't like it.
- Well, I'll take it anyway.

119
00:11:41,698 --> 00:11:43,325
Beggars can't be choosers
can they?

120
00:11:43,742 --> 00:11:44,784
No, they can't.

121
00:11:48,622 --> 00:11:49,956
Do you wanna join me?

122
00:11:52,042 --> 00:11:53,084
Sure.

123
00:11:55,086 --> 00:11:56,254
Patrick.

124
00:11:56,463 --> 00:11:57,964
- Kim.
- Hi.

125
00:12:00,675 --> 00:12:02,844
So you're from the, uh, southeast?

126
00:12:03,595 --> 00:12:04,638
Virginia?

127
00:12:05,305 --> 00:12:06,348
Good ear.

128
00:12:06,765 --> 00:12:07,807
You?

129
00:12:07,933 --> 00:12:09,935
Well, I... I lived all over.
Right now I live here.

130
00:12:11,228 --> 00:12:12,562
I was on the other side of the Island

131
00:12:12,687 --> 00:12:15,232
but people told me the beaches
on this side were better.

132
00:12:15,398 --> 00:12:17,192
- That's true.
- You here with your wife?

133
00:12:17,359 --> 00:12:18,401
No, just me.

134
00:12:19,277 --> 00:12:21,863
Oh, yeah, no. My wife, uh...

135
00:12:23,698 --> 00:12:25,909
Uh... not married anymore.

136
00:12:26,618 --> 00:12:28,787
- You?
- Me? No.

137
00:12:30,121 --> 00:12:34,542
Great. I mean, it's great if you...
If you like not being married...

138
00:12:34,668 --> 00:12:35,835
being single.

139
00:12:36,294 --> 00:12:37,420
- I do.
- Great.

140
00:12:37,754 --> 00:12:40,382
- "Thank you very much."
- "Yes, welcome."

141
00:13:06,172 --> 00:13:08,299
I came here to get away
to think about things.

142
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,951
What are you thinking about?

143
00:13:10,410 --> 00:13:14,414
I've been offered a promotion at work
but I'm not sure I want it.

144
00:13:14,539 --> 00:13:17,792
- Why is that?
- Oh... It's more work.

145
00:13:18,167 --> 00:13:19,377
It's more hassle.

146
00:13:20,336 --> 00:13:22,547
Eh, more money, but is it worth it?

147
00:13:23,548 --> 00:13:26,134
Well, sounds like you're asking yourself
the right questions.

148
00:13:26,551 --> 00:13:28,386
Must be strange to live here.

149
00:13:29,345 --> 00:13:30,888
It's so beautiful. I...

150
00:13:32,223 --> 00:13:33,975
I think if I were here full-time

151
00:13:34,225 --> 00:13:36,394
I'd feel like I was living in some kind
of dream world, you know?

152
00:13:36,561 --> 00:13:37,937
Ah, sometimes it's like that.

153
00:13:38,396 --> 00:13:40,523
There's nothing wrong
with dream worlds, right?

154
00:13:41,232 --> 00:13:43,276
- You're here to stay.
- Maybe.

155
00:13:45,028 --> 00:13:46,529
Man of mystery.

156
00:13:48,156 --> 00:13:49,198
Really?

157
00:13:49,866 --> 00:13:51,701
I don't mean to be mysterious.

158
00:13:53,953 --> 00:13:55,079
My wife died.

159
00:13:56,622 --> 00:13:59,042
Some things happened.
I did some things, and...

160
00:14:01,002 --> 00:14:02,754
I don't really know
how to talk about it yet.

161
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:06,299
I guess that's why
I still wear the ring.

162
00:14:07,675 --> 00:14:09,802
I'm just... Not ready.

163
00:14:10,595 --> 00:14:11,929
I think I understand.

164
00:14:13,765 --> 00:14:15,099
Anyway, that's why I'm here.

165
00:14:16,392 --> 00:14:18,061
It's not a bad place to be.

166
00:14:18,686 --> 00:14:22,106
- Right? It's beautiful.
- It's paradise.

167
00:14:22,523 --> 00:14:23,775
Exactly.

168
00:14:29,864 --> 00:14:30,907
Morning.

169
00:14:34,035 --> 00:14:35,453
Hi.

170
00:14:35,578 --> 00:14:36,621
Do you speak English?

171
00:14:36,746 --> 00:14:38,081
Yes, sir. I speak
very good, sir.

172
00:14:38,206 --> 00:14:39,707
Ah. Good.
What's your name?

173
00:14:40,291 --> 00:14:42,043
Morales.
Franklin Morales, sir.

174
00:14:42,835 --> 00:14:44,587
- Morales, huh?
- Mm.

175
00:14:44,837 --> 00:14:46,130
Have you seen this guy?

176
00:14:47,006 --> 00:14:48,049
No, sir.

177
00:14:49,050 --> 00:14:50,093
Okay then.

178
00:14:51,302 --> 00:14:52,762
- If you see him...
- Mm-hmm.

179
00:14:53,137 --> 00:14:55,056
- You'll tell me, yes?
- Yes, sir.

180
00:14:55,181 --> 00:14:56,349
- All right.
- Mm-hmm.

181
00:14:57,183 --> 00:14:58,810
- "Thank you very much."
- Mm-hmm.

182
00:14:59,519 --> 00:15:00,603
All right, fellas, let's get settled

183
00:15:00,728 --> 00:15:01,979
then we'll go get
something to eat.

184
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:04,065
Hey, Roger, what's up?

185
00:15:04,357 --> 00:15:05,525
"Thank you."

186
00:15:06,025 --> 00:15:07,944
Roger, Kim.
Kim, Roger.

187
00:15:08,069 --> 00:15:12,532
- Hi.
- My eyes were... Fluid cobras.

188
00:15:13,074 --> 00:15:14,742
Yeah. Good to see you.

189
00:15:16,035 --> 00:15:17,245
How long has he been here?

190
00:15:17,537 --> 00:15:19,455
Uh, not sure. Long time.

191
00:15:20,081 --> 00:15:21,249
You can tell.

192
00:15:21,916 --> 00:15:23,084
"One moment."

193
00:15:24,168 --> 00:15:25,211
Jane.

194
00:15:28,881 --> 00:15:30,508
Oh. Uh, excuse me.

195
00:15:34,345 --> 00:15:35,388
Hello?

196
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:37,598
- It's Franklin.
- Hey, Franklin. What's up?

197
00:15:37,723 --> 00:15:39,559
Three big American police
checked in.

198
00:15:39,892 --> 00:15:40,977
Looking for you.

199
00:15:41,769 --> 00:15:45,106
- Hmm. They're there now?
- Yes.

200
00:15:46,941 --> 00:15:48,734
Okay, well, see what else
you can find out.

201
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:51,446
- I'll be in touch, okay?
- Yes, of course.

202
00:15:52,113 --> 00:15:53,156
Bye.

203
00:16:00,371 --> 00:16:01,456
Is everything all right?

204
00:16:01,706 --> 00:16:03,833
Uh, yeah. Fine.
Uh, just some...

205
00:16:03,958 --> 00:16:05,543
Some people who wanna
meet with me.

206
00:16:05,751 --> 00:16:07,003
Listen, I have to head
back up to town.

207
00:16:07,128 --> 00:16:08,921
- Do you wanna come with me?
- Sure.

208
00:16:10,298 --> 00:16:11,382
See you around.

209
00:16:11,883 --> 00:16:13,301
- I'm sure I will.
- Bye.

210
00:16:34,238 --> 00:16:35,907
- That's a nice shirt.
- Thanks.

211
00:16:42,038 --> 00:16:43,414
Well, this was nice.

212
00:16:44,207 --> 00:16:45,917
I know you have people to see.

213
00:16:46,042 --> 00:16:48,586
Yes, uh, unfortunately
I do, yeah.

214
00:16:48,753 --> 00:16:49,795
No problem.

215
00:16:50,588 --> 00:16:52,006
Um, but I was wondering...

216
00:16:52,131 --> 00:16:54,967
Do you, uh, know a good
place around here for dinner?

217
00:16:59,096 --> 00:17:02,058
- Are you asking me out for dinner?
- Yeah.

218
00:17:03,142 --> 00:17:05,686
I figure you'll know a good
place where the locals go.

219
00:17:05,937 --> 00:17:07,855
Yeah, uh, I do. Um...

220
00:17:08,147 --> 00:17:09,190
Yes, I do...

221
00:17:11,567 --> 00:17:13,903
Well, why don't we meet here
at, uh...

222
00:17:14,445 --> 00:17:16,531
Oh, I don't know... eight?

223
00:17:17,198 --> 00:17:18,616
- Deal.
- Okay.

224
00:17:19,408 --> 00:17:21,410
- Eight o'clock.
- See ya then.

225
00:17:22,828 --> 00:17:25,081
The man who asks about you
is Abbott.

226
00:17:25,790 --> 00:17:27,291
That is the name
on the register.

227
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,335
Hmm. Where is he now?

228
00:17:29,835 --> 00:17:32,213
Eating. The other two men
are with him, but they leave.

229
00:17:32,463 --> 00:17:34,674
- Ah. Thank you.
- Mm-hmm.

230
00:17:34,966 --> 00:17:36,008
Thank you.

231
00:17:36,133 --> 00:17:37,176
Who's that guy?

232
00:17:37,426 --> 00:17:38,511
Danny Otero.

233
00:17:38,678 --> 00:17:39,720
Sells drugs.

234
00:17:40,096 --> 00:17:42,139
Comes here to buy heroin
from Vietnamese.

235
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:43,724
Bad business.

236
00:17:44,267 --> 00:17:47,853
How you say? Um...
Lousy Tipper.

237
00:17:48,271 --> 00:17:49,313
Lousy Tipper.

238
00:17:49,438 --> 00:17:50,898
Yeah. Yeah.

239
00:17:51,232 --> 00:17:52,400
Lousy Tipper.

240
00:17:56,737 --> 00:17:57,780
Abbott.

241
00:17:58,906 --> 00:18:00,157
How the heck are you?

242
00:18:03,744 --> 00:18:05,705
And here we thought
we were gonna have to turn over

243
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:08,082
every rock on this Island
to find you.

244
00:18:09,041 --> 00:18:10,209
I heard you were here.

245
00:18:10,626 --> 00:18:12,962
Well, it's only polite
to stop by and say hi.

246
00:18:13,296 --> 00:18:14,338
Hmm.

247
00:18:14,630 --> 00:18:15,965
Oh, how was the flight?

248
00:18:17,049 --> 00:18:18,092
Bumpy.

249
00:18:19,552 --> 00:18:22,013
Pretty confident of you
to front up like this.

250
00:18:22,638 --> 00:18:25,558
The extradition laws are on my side.
I know you can't touch me.

251
00:18:25,683 --> 00:18:27,101
Who said I wanted
to touch you?

252
00:18:27,810 --> 00:18:29,854
- I'm here to make you an offer.
- Oh.

253
00:18:30,646 --> 00:18:32,189
The powers-that-be

254
00:18:32,315 --> 00:18:36,193
decided that you
could be valuable to the FBI.

255
00:18:37,153 --> 00:18:40,114
The Bureau is willing to drop
all the charges against you

256
00:18:40,448 --> 00:18:41,824
if you come and work for us.

257
00:18:42,283 --> 00:18:43,451
For the FBI?

258
00:18:44,243 --> 00:18:45,369
That's right.

259
00:18:50,708 --> 00:18:51,917
There are the terms.

260
00:18:52,752 --> 00:18:54,879
You know, I wanna be very clear.

261
00:18:55,338 --> 00:18:56,756
I don't like this deal.

262
00:18:57,423 --> 00:18:59,050
If it were up to me
you would be headed home

263
00:18:59,175 --> 00:19:01,260
in a cargo plane
with a sack over your head.

264
00:19:02,011 --> 00:19:03,846
But, hey, I'm just the messenger.

265
00:19:04,180 --> 00:19:07,558
Interesting proposition.
I'm not buying it.

266
00:19:07,808 --> 00:19:08,851
No?

267
00:19:12,897 --> 00:19:14,690
Whatever my feelings are
about it...

268
00:19:16,192 --> 00:19:17,777
This is a good deal, Jane.

269
00:19:18,319 --> 00:19:20,071
You really need to consider it.

270
00:19:22,114 --> 00:19:24,575
I am done with that life.

271
00:19:25,159 --> 00:19:26,994
I did what I had to do

272
00:19:27,703 --> 00:19:28,913
and I've moved on.

273
00:19:29,789 --> 00:19:32,750
That life was a job
that you were very good at.

274
00:19:36,587 --> 00:19:38,631
If you come back, you can
help a lot of people.

275
00:19:39,465 --> 00:19:40,508
You have a gift.

276
00:19:41,175 --> 00:19:42,551
It's not a gift.

277
00:19:44,011 --> 00:19:46,013
Whatever it is, it'll
get you off this Island

278
00:19:46,138 --> 00:19:48,182
and you can start
your life again.

279
00:19:48,683 --> 00:19:50,685
I have. Thank you.

280
00:19:53,145 --> 00:19:54,188
Okay.

281
00:20:00,444 --> 00:20:02,905
We'll be here for another day
if you change your mind.

282
00:20:03,364 --> 00:20:04,490
How'd you find me?

283
00:20:06,659 --> 00:20:08,661
The letters to your girlfriend Lisbon.

284
00:20:09,578 --> 00:20:12,998
You know, it was pretty smart
to send them to your carny friends

285
00:20:13,124 --> 00:20:14,959
and have them sneak them
over to her.

286
00:20:16,085 --> 00:20:17,753
Just not quite smart enough.

287
00:20:21,465 --> 00:20:24,343
So I finally managed
to hack through the firewall

288
00:20:24,468 --> 00:20:26,178
and it turns out

289
00:20:26,303 --> 00:20:30,307
the cyber mastermind stealing credit card
numbers is an 11-year-old from Minneapolis.

290
00:20:30,433 --> 00:20:31,475
What?

291
00:20:31,642 --> 00:20:33,227
Yeah. He was
selling them to his friends

292
00:20:33,352 --> 00:20:35,730
so they could buy
limited-edition sneakers.

293
00:20:35,938 --> 00:20:37,523
- Did he get arrested?
- I don't know.

294
00:20:37,648 --> 00:20:39,608
We turned the information
over to the Minneapolis PD.

295
00:20:39,734 --> 00:20:40,901
Actually, they did.

296
00:20:41,068 --> 00:20:42,111
I checked.

297
00:20:42,236 --> 00:20:44,363
- And he's gonna be tried as a juvenile.
- Oh, well, there you go.

298
00:21:08,095 --> 00:21:10,806
So the digital surveillance
company is going well, huh?

299
00:21:10,931 --> 00:21:14,435
Yeah. We've been up and running now
for, uh, 15 months, and...

300
00:21:15,019 --> 00:21:16,937
already turning a tidy profit
believe it or not.

301
00:21:17,062 --> 00:21:18,314
- Yeah.
- Nice.

302
00:21:18,647 --> 00:21:19,815
How are things here?

303
00:21:20,608 --> 00:21:24,487
Same. You know, it's mostly
DUIs, stolen bikes...

304
00:21:24,612 --> 00:21:25,863
But I like it that way.

305
00:21:26,238 --> 00:21:27,740
It's nice and quiet.

306
00:21:28,282 --> 00:21:29,700
It's the babysitter.
Excuse me.

307
00:21:29,867 --> 00:21:30,910
Hello?

308
00:21:31,952 --> 00:21:33,454
Maddy's got a slight fever.

309
00:21:35,206 --> 00:21:36,957
Grace worries. I try
and tell her it's nothing.

310
00:21:37,082 --> 00:21:39,627
- But first baby, you know?
- Sure.

311
00:21:41,086 --> 00:21:43,088
- Can I ask you something, Wayne?
- Mm.

312
00:21:45,466 --> 00:21:47,510
- Do you ever miss the CBI?
- Hmm.

313
00:21:49,094 --> 00:21:51,180
Sure. Sometimes.

314
00:21:51,722 --> 00:21:52,973
I mean, Grace and I are so busy.

315
00:21:53,682 --> 00:21:55,309
I don't really have much time
to think about it.

316
00:21:55,434 --> 00:21:57,436
- Things are so hectic.
- Hmm.

317
00:21:58,896 --> 00:22:01,190
I used to miss it, but not anymore.

318
00:22:01,982 --> 00:22:04,109
Yeah. Everything here's good.

319
00:22:04,860 --> 00:22:06,695
You know, it's just...
it's good.

320
00:22:06,987 --> 00:22:10,574
- That's great, boss.
- I am not your boss anymore.

321
00:22:11,325 --> 00:22:13,202
She says her fever's up to 102.7.

322
00:22:13,327 --> 00:22:15,162
Oh. I'm sorry.
We're out of here.

323
00:22:15,287 --> 00:22:17,039
- I'm so sorry.
- No, it's fine.

324
00:22:17,206 --> 00:22:18,666
But I'll walk you to your car.

325
00:22:19,959 --> 00:22:23,337
So... those people
that wanted to meet with you.

326
00:22:23,462 --> 00:22:24,964
- Did you meet with them?
- Yeah.

327
00:22:26,382 --> 00:22:27,424
How'd it go?

328
00:22:29,176 --> 00:22:30,511
Uh, it was interesting.

329
00:22:30,719 --> 00:22:32,555
They made me a job offer.

330
00:22:33,013 --> 00:22:34,056
Hmm?

331
00:22:35,391 --> 00:22:39,186
Basically, if I go and work for them
then I can go back to the US.

332
00:22:40,062 --> 00:22:41,146
Sounds good.

333
00:22:41,856 --> 00:22:42,898
Not really.

334
00:22:43,816 --> 00:22:45,317
I've kind of moved on.

335
00:22:46,569 --> 00:22:48,195
It would be going backwards.

336
00:22:50,948 --> 00:22:52,241
And I don't think that's healthy.

337
00:22:54,952 --> 00:22:57,955
What is it that you... do, anyway?

338
00:22:58,414 --> 00:23:00,499
- What do I do?
- Yeah.

339
00:23:03,210 --> 00:23:05,045
I, uh... I look for people.

340
00:23:06,171 --> 00:23:08,924
- Sounds intriguing.
- It is. Was.

341
00:23:10,759 --> 00:23:11,802
It was fun.

342
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:14,305
Still, you get to go home.

343
00:23:15,222 --> 00:23:16,807
Aren't there things that you miss?

344
00:23:17,057 --> 00:23:18,309
Sure, of course.

345
00:23:22,521 --> 00:23:23,731
Thank you for this.

346
00:23:25,065 --> 00:23:28,193
I needed the company.
I didn't think I did, but, uh...

347
00:23:29,904 --> 00:23:32,698
Ah, it turns out that... I do.

348
00:23:34,909 --> 00:23:35,951
Who doesn't?

349
00:23:41,790 --> 00:23:43,083
You wanna go dancing?

350
00:23:44,627 --> 00:23:45,669
Yeah.

351
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,348
It's a beautiful night.

352
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,766
It is.

353
00:24:43,394 --> 00:24:45,104
I think there's somebody
following us.

354
00:24:47,606 --> 00:24:49,316
- I'll just go and talk to them.
- No! Patrick!

355
00:24:49,441 --> 00:24:50,484
- Come on.
- No, it's okay. It's fine.

356
00:24:50,609 --> 00:24:51,652
I speak the lingo.

357
00:24:52,152 --> 00:24:54,947
- What are you...
- Hey, guys, come out where I can see you.

358
00:24:55,364 --> 00:24:56,907
Let's have a...
Whoa...

359
00:24:59,326 --> 00:25:00,619
Oh, my God.

360
00:25:05,249 --> 00:25:06,458
Patrick?

361
00:25:21,638 --> 00:25:22,806
Ah...

362
00:25:23,557 --> 00:25:24,850
That feels good.

363
00:25:26,768 --> 00:25:28,186
You smell nice.

364
00:25:29,813 --> 00:25:33,525
- You should see a doctor.
- No... No.

365
00:25:33,650 --> 00:25:35,318
You could have a concussion.

366
00:25:36,278 --> 00:25:38,780
Nah, I just...
Just need to rest.

367
00:26:35,087 --> 00:26:37,547
I was very, uh, drunk last night.

368
00:26:38,006 --> 00:26:39,174
Yes.

369
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:41,093
What happened?

370
00:26:41,301 --> 00:26:42,677
You got beat up.

371
00:26:43,220 --> 00:26:44,262
Here.

372
00:26:45,138 --> 00:26:46,264
Thank you.

373
00:26:54,856 --> 00:26:56,566
Oh, that is so good.

374
00:26:58,068 --> 00:26:59,236
How are you feeling?

375
00:27:00,028 --> 00:27:02,155
Better now, after this.

376
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:05,700
- You make good tea.
- Thank you.

377
00:27:07,619 --> 00:27:09,121
I got a text this morning.

378
00:27:09,955 --> 00:27:12,249
My work.
I have to go back today.

379
00:27:12,791 --> 00:27:15,293
I have a midday flight
and I have to pack, and...

380
00:27:15,752 --> 00:27:18,588
Yeah, I understand.
You gotta go back.

381
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:23,218
- Yeah. Sorry.
- Oh, no, it's... it's fine.

382
00:27:24,136 --> 00:27:25,387
Thanks for everything.

383
00:27:30,767 --> 00:27:31,810
Oh...

384
00:27:35,772 --> 00:27:37,732
I really had a wonderful time
with you, Patrick.

385
00:27:38,024 --> 00:27:39,067
Mm.

386
00:27:40,193 --> 00:27:41,319
Anyway...

387
00:28:10,515 --> 00:28:11,766
Hugo!

388
00:28:28,241 --> 00:28:29,492
Alfredo?

389
00:28:42,672 --> 00:28:44,049
What happened?

390
00:28:54,851 --> 00:28:55,977
Pow.

391
00:29:31,513 --> 00:29:32,555
Hey.

392
00:29:33,556 --> 00:29:34,599
Hi.

393
00:29:34,724 --> 00:29:35,767
I was hoping
I'd find you here.

394
00:29:36,434 --> 00:29:37,978
I wanted to give you something.

395
00:29:38,979 --> 00:29:40,105
Oh, thank you.

396
00:29:40,355 --> 00:29:43,066
No, thank you...
for dinner and everything.

397
00:29:43,191 --> 00:29:45,443
I...
You're right.

398
00:29:46,152 --> 00:29:48,863
Being understood
is an underrated pleasure.

399
00:29:50,240 --> 00:29:51,825
Let me give you my home
phone number

400
00:29:51,950 --> 00:29:54,327
in case you ever make it
back to the States.

401
00:29:56,288 --> 00:29:57,330
You never know.

402
00:29:57,914 --> 00:29:59,165
You might wanna give me a call.

403
00:30:00,583 --> 00:30:01,626
I might.

404
00:30:04,462 --> 00:30:05,797
Goodbye, Patrick.

405
00:30:06,923 --> 00:30:08,341
Good luck with your decision.

406
00:30:09,676 --> 00:30:10,719
You know, one thing...

407
00:30:10,844 --> 00:30:12,762
Going back doesn't have
to mean going backwards.

408
00:30:13,346 --> 00:30:14,723
It can mean moving on.

409
00:31:26,711 --> 00:31:28,630
- Abbott.
- Hey, G-man.

410
00:31:30,590 --> 00:31:35,053
- I'm ready to come home.
- Wow. That is good news.

411
00:31:35,220 --> 00:31:37,722
But on my terms.
Is that clear?

412
00:31:38,181 --> 00:31:39,224
And when we get back
to the US

413
00:31:39,349 --> 00:31:41,226
I want a meeting with
whatever powers-that-be

414
00:31:41,351 --> 00:31:44,312
to make clear that those
are the terms.

415
00:31:44,562 --> 00:31:46,356
I'm sure we can work out
something like that.

416
00:31:46,523 --> 00:31:48,066
- And I want Lisbon there.
- "Why?"

417
00:31:48,358 --> 00:31:50,610
Lisbon's there, or I don't do it.

418
00:31:50,777 --> 00:31:52,821
And if you say she's gonna
be there, and she's not

419
00:31:53,238 --> 00:31:54,697
I will make it clear to your bosses

420
00:31:54,823 --> 00:31:57,951
that I will work
with any FBI agent except you.

421
00:31:59,202 --> 00:32:02,205
You'll have done all the work to get me
and get nothing for it.

422
00:32:03,415 --> 00:32:04,749
Do we have an understanding?

423
00:32:05,375 --> 00:32:07,085
What time do you want us
to pick you up?

424
00:32:07,460 --> 00:32:08,628
I'll let you know.

425
00:32:09,212 --> 00:32:10,755
I got something I gotta do first.

426
00:32:13,466 --> 00:32:15,718
- "Franklin?"
- Patrick? How are you?

427
00:32:15,885 --> 00:32:17,720
Good. I'm very good.
Uh, I need your help.

428
00:32:17,929 --> 00:32:20,181
You said that Danny Otero
was buying some heroin

429
00:32:20,306 --> 00:32:21,766
from some Vietnamese dealers.

430
00:32:21,891 --> 00:32:23,935
You should have nothing to do
with Danny Otero.

431
00:32:24,102 --> 00:32:26,062
Me? No, of course not.
I'm not going anywhere near him.

432
00:32:26,563 --> 00:32:28,148
Do you know if he's already
made the buy?

433
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:31,317
No. No, Vietnamese guests
only check in this morning.

434
00:32:31,443 --> 00:32:34,946
Excellent. I need you
to find out three things for me.

435
00:32:35,363 --> 00:32:36,739
I can find out anything.

436
00:32:36,990 --> 00:32:39,367
First, when will the deal happen?

437
00:32:39,617 --> 00:32:41,953
Second, what room
will they be in?

438
00:32:42,162 --> 00:32:43,204
What else?

439
00:32:43,329 --> 00:32:44,372
Uh, yes.

440
00:32:44,497 --> 00:32:46,040
Uh, when the Vietnamese
will be eating.

441
00:32:46,374 --> 00:32:49,043
No problem. They never eat.
Always in the bar.

442
00:32:49,294 --> 00:32:51,838
Excellent, Franklin.
You're very good.

443
00:32:52,213 --> 00:32:53,798
Very, very good.

444
00:32:54,132 --> 00:32:55,175
Thank you.

445
00:33:03,183 --> 00:33:04,309
"Thank you."

446
00:33:13,276 --> 00:33:16,070
Good afternoon.
Sorry for the interruption.

447
00:33:16,196 --> 00:33:19,115
Uh, I assume one of you
speaks English.

448
00:33:21,409 --> 00:33:22,452
I do.

449
00:33:22,577 --> 00:33:24,245
Patrick Jane.
Pleased to meet you.

450
00:33:24,537 --> 00:33:25,788
What's this about?

451
00:33:27,790 --> 00:33:29,918
I know you're drug dealers.
I don't judge.

452
00:33:30,168 --> 00:33:32,212
I'm wanted for homicide
myself in the US.

453
00:33:32,462 --> 00:33:35,173
what I wanna discuss
is a mutual acquaintance...

454
00:33:35,298 --> 00:33:36,466
Danny Otero.

455
00:33:38,801 --> 00:33:39,844
What about him?

456
00:33:40,845 --> 00:33:42,931
Well, I thought I should
warn you. He's flipped.

457
00:33:43,389 --> 00:33:45,850
He's working as an informer
to the police.

458
00:33:46,059 --> 00:33:49,479
He's teamed up with an FBI
agent named Abbott.

459
00:33:54,025 --> 00:33:55,068
How do you know this?

460
00:33:55,193 --> 00:33:57,904
Well, I'm working with Abbott myself
on a different deal.

461
00:33:58,029 --> 00:33:59,989
That's how Otero's name came up.

462
00:34:00,365 --> 00:34:02,742
If you have any business
with Danny Otero

463
00:34:02,992 --> 00:34:04,077
word to the wise...

464
00:34:04,619 --> 00:34:05,995
You might wanna be careful.

465
00:34:09,624 --> 00:34:10,667
See ya.

466
00:34:15,630 --> 00:34:16,673
Abbott.

467
00:34:17,090 --> 00:34:20,468
I'll be in room 1443
in 15 minutes.

468
00:34:20,677 --> 00:34:21,719
Here in the hotel?

469
00:34:21,844 --> 00:34:24,180
I'm having a little goodbye drink
with some friends.

470
00:34:24,472 --> 00:34:27,475
Just identify yourself at the door
And they'll come get me.

471
00:34:40,863 --> 00:34:41,906
Yes?

472
00:34:42,532 --> 00:34:44,951
Abbott. FBI.

473
00:34:45,660 --> 00:34:46,703
Excuse me?

474
00:34:47,245 --> 00:34:48,413
Abbott, FBI.

475
00:34:48,538 --> 00:34:50,123
Didn't Patrick Jane
tell you I was coming?

476
00:34:52,166 --> 00:34:53,209
One moment.

477
00:35:05,930 --> 00:35:08,391
- Did you sell us to the police?
- What?

478
00:35:08,516 --> 00:35:09,892
Did you sell us to the police?

479
00:35:10,351 --> 00:35:11,394
No, no, no...

480
00:35:12,604 --> 00:35:14,105
The feds are right outside.
The FBI.

481
00:35:15,982 --> 00:35:17,191
"You think you can get away
with this?"

482
00:35:18,067 --> 00:35:19,611
The hell with this.
All right...

483
00:35:19,819 --> 00:35:21,696
- I'm telling you, I'm not...
- FBI! Don't move!

484
00:35:21,821 --> 00:35:22,864
Don't move!

485
00:35:23,072 --> 00:35:24,365
Put your hands on your head.

486
00:35:25,366 --> 00:35:26,534
Put the gun down.

487
00:35:27,619 --> 00:35:29,704
"Leave that... Now."

488
00:35:32,498 --> 00:35:34,876
Good job. All right. Now everybody get down
on the ground.

489
00:35:35,209 --> 00:35:37,253
Down on the ground.

490
00:35:37,754 --> 00:35:38,880
"To the ground."

491
00:35:40,757 --> 00:35:42,091
"On your stomach."

492
00:35:42,884 --> 00:35:43,926
Huh?

493
00:35:47,138 --> 00:35:48,389
Ah, that's nice.

494
00:35:49,057 --> 00:35:50,350
Very nice.

495
00:35:51,643 --> 00:35:53,102
The only question is...

496
00:35:54,395 --> 00:35:56,147
Where's Patrick Jane?

497
00:36:06,824 --> 00:36:08,409
Abbott, what happened?

498
00:36:12,538 --> 00:36:13,873
You set this up.

499
00:36:14,207 --> 00:36:15,875
You're the one
who knocked on the door.

500
00:36:17,460 --> 00:36:18,503
My terms.

501
00:36:19,045 --> 00:36:21,673
I need you to read them
and sign it.

502
00:36:29,138 --> 00:36:31,849
- We can work with this.
- Excellent. Sign it, please.

503
00:36:37,313 --> 00:36:38,356
All right.

504
00:36:38,481 --> 00:36:39,524
Five more copies.

505
00:36:39,649 --> 00:36:40,900
Sign those, too, please.

506
00:36:42,318 --> 00:36:43,403
They're for you.

507
00:36:43,903 --> 00:36:45,196
I keep the original.

508
00:36:49,909 --> 00:36:51,786
- All right. Let's go.
- Ah, one second.

509
00:36:59,544 --> 00:37:00,628
Now we can go.

510
00:37:08,344 --> 00:37:09,470
Mr. Jane!

511
00:38:37,890 --> 00:38:38,933
Jane.

512
00:38:40,017 --> 00:38:41,060
Cho.

513
00:38:42,102 --> 00:38:43,145
Ha!

514
00:38:43,270 --> 00:38:44,730
You never cease to amaze me.

515
00:38:46,232 --> 00:38:47,483
I got him from here, guys.

516
00:38:50,694 --> 00:38:52,154
So you joined the FBI, huh?

517
00:38:52,696 --> 00:38:53,739
Yeah.

518
00:38:53,864 --> 00:38:55,616
Finished training
at Quantico five months ago.

519
00:38:56,617 --> 00:38:58,577
Wow. Look at you.

520
00:38:59,119 --> 00:39:00,788
- Congratulations.
- Thanks.

521
00:39:01,705 --> 00:39:02,748
Yeah.

522
00:39:04,583 --> 00:39:06,085
- It's this way.
- Okay.

523
00:39:10,965 --> 00:39:12,174
Where are your socks?

524
00:39:12,842 --> 00:39:15,803
Uh... I don't know.

525
00:39:17,847 --> 00:39:19,306
Did they put a chip
in your neck?

526
00:39:19,431 --> 00:39:21,183
Not that I know of.
Why do you ask?

527
00:39:22,142 --> 00:39:23,978
Ah, you just don't seem
too happy to see me.

528
00:39:24,144 --> 00:39:25,354
I am happy to see you.

529
00:39:25,479 --> 00:39:26,897
I just wish it was under
different circumstances.

530
00:39:27,022 --> 00:39:28,065
Why is that?

531
00:39:28,190 --> 00:39:29,817
I don't think you and the FBI
are gonna get along very well.

532
00:39:30,025 --> 00:39:31,569
I don't think they really
understand how you operate.

533
00:39:31,819 --> 00:39:34,405
Ah. They'll loosen up
once they get to know me.

534
00:39:34,530 --> 00:39:35,573
Mm-hmm.

535
00:39:35,698 --> 00:39:36,907
Second door on the left.

536
00:39:49,211 --> 00:39:50,254
Hey.

537
00:39:50,796 --> 00:39:51,881
Hello.

538
00:39:53,465 --> 00:39:54,758
Nice beard.

539
00:39:54,967 --> 00:39:56,010
Thank you.

540
00:39:56,135 --> 00:39:57,428
Thank you for the letters.

541
00:39:57,595 --> 00:39:58,804
Oh, I missed you.

542
00:39:59,471 --> 00:40:00,973
I missed you, too.

543
00:40:06,020 --> 00:40:07,897
What's going on, huh?
Why am I here?

544
00:40:08,022 --> 00:40:10,482
- You'll see. It's gonna be great.
- What?

545
00:40:10,608 --> 00:40:11,775
Trust me.

546
00:40:13,277 --> 00:40:15,613
All right, let's get this started.

547
00:40:20,701 --> 00:40:25,080
Jane... these are the charges
pending against you...

548
00:40:25,331 --> 00:40:27,458
Homicide, obstruction of justice

549
00:40:27,625 --> 00:40:30,920
aggravated assault
grand theft auto, etcetera.

550
00:40:32,379 --> 00:40:33,839
You're looking at 20 to life.

551
00:40:34,298 --> 00:40:35,799
But all of that can go away

552
00:40:36,050 --> 00:40:41,555
if you agree to serve as a consultant
for the FBI for at least five years.

553
00:40:42,765 --> 00:40:46,101
You will be under my supervision
on federal parole

554
00:40:46,226 --> 00:40:50,439
which may be revoked
at any time at my discretion.

555
00:40:50,856 --> 00:40:54,109
You screw up, run away
do anything that I don't like

556
00:40:54,860 --> 00:40:56,403
and you'll be in the jailhouse.

557
00:40:59,365 --> 00:41:00,783
Sign, and we have a deal.

558
00:41:03,077 --> 00:41:04,119
Interesting.

559
00:41:05,621 --> 00:41:07,581
As you're aware

560
00:41:07,748 --> 00:41:11,627
you have already agreed
to some terms.

561
00:41:12,419 --> 00:41:14,129
I didn't agree to those.

562
00:41:15,214 --> 00:41:17,424
I signed indicating that I read them.

563
00:41:17,549 --> 00:41:19,760
- Same difference.
- No, it's not, believe me.

564
00:41:19,885 --> 00:41:23,138
Firstly, no parole.
I'm a free man.

565
00:41:23,305 --> 00:41:25,766
And secondly
Lisbon has to work with me.

566
00:41:25,891 --> 00:41:27,726
- Hey, hello?
- Well, you won't need Lisbon.

567
00:41:27,851 --> 00:41:29,395
I've already assembled a team
to work with you.

568
00:41:29,520 --> 00:41:31,647
- Oh, that's not negotiable.
- I have a job, okay?

569
00:41:31,772 --> 00:41:32,815
I'm not gonna drop everything

570
00:41:32,940 --> 00:41:34,817
just because you suddenly
decided to come back.

571
00:41:34,942 --> 00:41:35,985
W... we'll talk.

572
00:41:36,110 --> 00:41:37,194
There are some other stipulations.

573
00:41:37,319 --> 00:41:38,946
Easy stuff.
I'm sure we can figure them out.

574
00:41:39,071 --> 00:41:41,532
But none of this applies.
This...

575
00:41:41,657 --> 00:41:44,868
I don't think you're hearing me, Jane.

576
00:41:46,370 --> 00:41:47,913
You are on US soil now.

577
00:41:48,038 --> 00:41:52,292
I am the federal government
and I am telling you that that is a napkin.

578
00:41:54,420 --> 00:41:57,047
This... is the deal.

579
00:41:57,798 --> 00:41:58,841
Take it...

580
00:41:59,550 --> 00:42:00,592
or leave it.

581
00:42:02,594 --> 00:42:05,347
- I'll leave it.
- Oh, that's too bad.

582
00:42:05,472 --> 00:42:07,016
You made a mistake,
but, hey...

583
00:42:07,975 --> 00:42:09,018
Kim?

584
00:42:09,727 --> 00:42:11,061
Agent Fischer.

585
00:42:11,395 --> 00:42:12,438
Kim?

586
00:42:12,730 --> 00:42:13,939
Agent Fischer.

587
00:42:16,734 --> 00:42:18,152
Agent Fischer.

588
00:42:20,362 --> 00:42:23,782
Mr. Jane will be going
to a detention suite.

589
00:42:23,949 --> 00:42:26,326
I'm sorry to hear that.
I'll make the arrangements.

590
00:42:26,577 --> 00:42:27,828
Oh, yeah, I'm not fussy.

591
00:42:28,412 --> 00:42:29,747
If you have one with a view
I'll take it.

592
00:42:29,872 --> 00:42:33,876
If not, uh, whatever
as long as I can make some tea.

593
00:42:35,586 --> 00:42:37,671
Who is she, and what is a detention suite?

594
00:42:37,796 --> 00:42:39,465
Don't worry, Lisbon.
It's all under control.


